#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188123 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b14ef98-8122-512a-9cce-6e44392959d8" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using Various Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "b0e16600-3365-562f-8cc8-bf25e0c1638a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3144" :question/problem "Express $\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1$ in terms of $\\sec x$ only." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} x = \\sec^{2} x \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} x = \\sec^{2} x - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{2} x = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan^{2} x\\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{4} x + 1 &= \\tan^{2} x(\\sec^{2} x - \\tan^{2} x) + 1 \\\\\n&= \\tan^{2} x \\cdot (1) + 1 \\\\\n&= \\tan^{2} x + 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can use $(1)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan^{2} x + 1 &= \\sec^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x\\sec^2 x - \\tan^4 x +1 = \\sec^2 x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188124 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eda44360-52ec-59f7-98b4-f8d866a465e9" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression Using the Alternate Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "91980d9e-0e4f-546e-b9ee-3117c4950aed" :question/math-academy-id "e-3455" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue} 1} = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec^2 \\theta - \\tan^2 \\theta} = 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188125 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "915ff3d9-c631-5134-82ff-58dbf0167602" :question/math-academy-id "e-3463" :question/problem "Simplify $\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the different forms of the secant-tangent Identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(1) & 1 + \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ \\\\ (2) & \\tan^{2} θ = \\sec^{2} θ - 1 \\\\ (3) & \\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ = 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can rewrite our expression using $(3)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{blue}1}{\\sec{\\theta}+\\tan{\\theta}} = \\dfrac{\\color{blue}\\sec^2{\\theta} - \\tan^2{\\theta}}{\\sec{\\theta} + \\tan{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we can further simplify our expression by factoring the numerator as a difference of squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sec^{2} θ - \\tan^{2} θ}{\\sec θ + \\tan θ} &= ((\\sec θ - \\tan θ)(\\sec θ + \\tan θ))/(\\sec θ + \\tan θ) \\\\\n&= ((\\sec θ - \\tan θ)(\\sec θ + \\tan θ))/((\\sec θ + \\tan θ)) \\\\\n&= \\sec θ - \\tan θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta} = \\sec{\\theta} - \\tan{\\theta}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188889 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "141d61c7-1d82-52fe-b977-19daa910da9b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring Alternative Forms of the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc77baf0-4469-503f-83a6-d2de86933824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187815} {:answer/id #uuid "e700d2fc-70b5-5a70-b0dd-3b3ea2254d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x + \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187816} {:answer/id #uuid "eaaddfa3-7d18-5664-bd11-d1c5e78c8bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sec x + \\tan x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187817} {:answer/id #uuid "eb07bb9a-bb2c-5948-870c-7b151292816a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- (\\sec x - \\tan x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187818} {:answer/id #uuid "234f9771-28c3-5e21-b971-7d49f78c6485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e700d2fc-70b5-5a70-b0dd-3b3ea2254d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x + \\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187816} :answer-field/id #uuid "39849032-fe5b-5aac-888e-42054128fb15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186187814}] :question/id #uuid "98997ad6-1ba3-510a-969b-b1a491e9f8b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-65392" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{1}{\\sec x - \\tan x}$."}]}
